{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Harris Corner Detector.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Harris Corner Detector.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"harris corner detector harris corner detector","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Harris Corner Detector.md","fileName":"Harris Corner Detector.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Harris Corner Detector","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 00:47\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Copy-Move and Resampling Forensics]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Copy-Move and Resampling Forensics","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Harris Corner Detector.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Harris Corner Detector.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"harris corner detector harris corner detector","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Harris Corner Detector.md","fileName":"Harris Corner Detector.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Harris Corner Detector","heading":"Harris Corner Detector","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The Harris corner detector identifies locations where image intensity changes strongly in two directions. Shifting a window around a true corner produces large differences for movements along either axis, unlike an edge, which changes mainly across one direction, or a flat patch, which changes little.\n\nThese stable points provide candidate locations for clone matching. The detector reduces the search space but does not determine whether a forgery occurred; descriptors, geometric grouping, and pixel-level verification must follow.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Copy-Move and Resampling Forensics","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Harris Corner Detector.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Harris Corner Detector.md","sourceType":"markd